From 00858f11f4ec049af394a235a5222e525307e0a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:19:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PermissionController: Use the RavenOS glass theme

Draw the Settings-style pages (Permission manager, each permission's
app list, an app's permissions and All permissions, the per-app
permission choices, Default apps and their pickers, Special app access)
like the RavenOS glass Settings:

- The Settings theme uses raven_backdrop as the window background, with
  transparent status, navigation and action bars, and reads every color
  from res/values/raven_glass.xml so a product overlay can recolor it.
- Add GlassGroupDecoration (ported from RavenOS Settings), which draws
  each preference group as one rounded glass card with inset separators
  in a centred column. PermissionsFrameFragment and the role
  SettingsFragment attach it, which covers every handheld page.
- Put the per-app permission choices in a glass card in the same centred
  column, and drop the rule under the app header.
- Keep dialogs on a solid surface, since Android 11 has no backdrop blur.

The runtime permission grant dialog is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I65ed5cda01daadde893a879e4e433836b9aca589
